<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Osona</h1><p class="st-meta">798 CE – 1111 CE (approx.) · capital Vic</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Catalan county of the plain of Vic, resettled by Wilfred the Hairy, where the monasteries of Ripoll and Vic grew into centres of learning.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Osona, named after the ancient <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ausetani">Ausetani</a>, came under Frankish rule around 798. After the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aisso">Aissó</a> in 826 it was largely abandoned. From about 879 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfred-the-hairy">Wilfred the Hairy</a> repopulated the plain of Vic, restored its bishopric in 886 and founded the monasteries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monastery-of-santa-maria-de-ripoll">Ripoll</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monastery-of-sant-joan-de-les-abadesses">Sant Joan de les Abadesses</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Osona was a frontier county facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, settled by free peasant colonists who cleared land and built castles. It was usually held by the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> rather than having its own line. Its church centres flourished: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monastery-of-santa-maria-de-ripoll">Ripoll</a>'s library made it a hub of learning in the 10th century, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-sylvester-ii">Gerbert of Aurillac</a> studied Arabic science.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Osona remained in the hands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-barcelona">House of Barcelona</a>, briefly granted to younger sons, until it was fully merged with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-barcelona">County of Barcelona</a>. It became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Catalonia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon</a>, and Vic remains its centre.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-osona.jpg" alt="County of Osona" width="320" height="410"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borrell.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>798 CE – 1111 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wilfred the Hairy, Borrell II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>County of Ausona, Comtat d'Osona</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=954&amp;focus=county-of-osona" aria-label="County of Osona on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4735 685 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Osona lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5055 941L5139 672M5055 941L5053 958"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5139 672h0M5053 958h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5055 941h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5055 941h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vic. <a href="/atlas?year=954&amp;focus=county-of-osona">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
